description:
Celebrate Matariki at Rawene Community Centre!
Dawn Matariki Star Art Activation | 5am - 7am&nbsp;
Begin the day with a pre-dawn Matariki gathering at Rawene, welcoming the rising of the stars through star-inspired artmaking, remembrance and intention-setting for the year ahead.&nbsp;
Kai and Wānanga e Hapori | 7am - 8am 
Following the dawn activation, the community will gather for light breakfast kai and a shared wānanga - a time for whakawhanaungatanga and kōrero in a welcoming setting.&nbsp;
Toi and Kaupapa Māori Workshops | 9am – 12 noon 
A series of free (or koha) hands-on workshops and activations celebrating toi Māori, mātauranga, language and community participation. All welcome!
